WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.130
1539: an ordinance makes French the
language of law and administration.

2
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.000
Late 19th century: free schooling,

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.570
in French only.

4
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.860
In many schools, pupils were punished
for speaking their regional language.

5
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.590
2008: the Constitution says regional languages
belong to the «patrimoine de la France».

6
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:27.090
And since 1977, «Diwan» schools
have taught pupils mostly in Breton.

7
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.370
So if these languages are heritage,

8
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.380
why can't a state school
teach mostly in them?

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.640
In this mission, you'll map
France's regional languages,

10
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.530
from Brittany to Corsica and overseas.

11
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.070
Then you'll sort heritage into national,

12
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.800
regional and local.

13
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.190
Your mission: find out why
state schools can't teach

14
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.120
mostly in a regional language.
